{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_0358f7208b37f35b4b2c2dc52e2eb0e9ec2efc298b72d5aaeeb6513523ebb8c0"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Marketplace sample outputs cannot be authored; they are auto-generated, with each input potentially producing up to five distinct outputs, to ensure intellectual honesty."},{"claim_ids":["clm_0c1c2fb61df6f062faea9465357efe991e6bd74faeff2b65247609a36a45ae3a"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: cartridges go in a `/cartridges` subfolder as YAML files; a recursive search finds them regardless of internal directory structure."},{"claim_ids":["clm_107c202059fb396e87b7af0312ce1fd4f01f6b9f3b993d89c7fd10b80088877d"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Running a Cartridge requires an external implementation; the repository itself does not provide one."},{"claim_ids":["clm_2b851d1538021a759fa45c10be76264010901326734e2a3170ab62a2aa930842"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The licensing section states it is uncertain whether its licensing approach is practical or enforceable, and that it should be seen as a statement of intention, not a guarantee."},{"claim_ids":["clm_8fa03a2ef3df44dc020571c5e824da75aa5af20a0625c45d6d43320cfc5ed9a0"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Cartridges may include a `miscellaneous.marketplace` section with `tags` (clean-URL style) and `samples` entries specifying interface type and inputs."},{"claim_ids":["clm_95cd47396e54bc8a7451ea63ca24f07e6412361971b9051398f80cecaeda58ea"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The project recommends authors publish cartridges under permissive licenses (CC0-1.0 preferred, any SPDX-known license allowed) given unresolved questions about prompt licensing."},{"claim_ids":["clm_a52685c907d49e825bc98da5a2f1834b090b33505e3dad4f02a1f7f9d4e1b260"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Cartridges can be used by downloading the YAML file or copying its contents into a local YAML file, then running it with an implementation."},{"claim_ids":["clm_ac0c2f8925aaeed30358a4d3b2e628443322d100ba9fdb924781f2c064143318"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Listed implementations include a Ruby CLI, a Clinic live editor, a Nano Bots API with a public endpoint, and Sublime Text and VS Code extensions."},{"claim_ids":["clm_be88594ecb6d256e77aa535a2d6a0684f60387e1780eb4d758d05ebe723e3bc8"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The repository hosts Nano Bots' Cartridges, which are YAML files that require a separate implementation to run."},{"claim_ids":["clm_c35d887b3559dc4429407dcb8ba1b31ba8f4baecb2e73bd8619585645b54e751"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: each user folder is tied to the contributor's GitHub username and only accepts pull requests from that user."},{"claim_ids":["clm_f4b2980acc287e4aa4fa03752919b29801bf8e46f8033e8b1d3cca54f89643e2"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: the README recommends studying existing cartridges in the repo and their nbots.io pages as a learning path, and points to the official spec documentation for creating cartridges."},{"claim_ids":["clm_f4be21367e82f5a823f128b2e5a362a05be6dfa898ee852e7b29544f2828e00b"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: contributors share Cartridges via pull request, creating a folder named `@your-nickname` under `/cartridges` with a `profile.yml` describing the author."}],"claim_ids":["clm_0358f7208b37f35b4b2c2dc52e2eb0e9ec2efc298b72d5aaeeb6513523ebb8c0","clm_0c1c2fb61df6f062faea9465357efe991e6bd74faeff2b65247609a36a45ae3a","clm_107c202059fb396e87b7af0312ce1fd4f01f6b9f3b993d89c7fd10b80088877d","clm_2b851d1538021a759fa45c10be76264010901326734e2a3170ab62a2aa930842","clm_8fa03a2ef3df44dc020571c5e824da75aa5af20a0625c45d6d43320cfc5ed9a0","clm_95cd47396e54bc8a7451ea63ca24f07e6412361971b9051398f80cecaeda58ea","clm_a52685c907d49e825bc98da5a2f1834b090b33505e3dad4f02a1f7f9d4e1b260","clm_ac0c2f8925aaeed30358a4d3b2e628443322d100ba9fdb924781f2c064143318","clm_be88594ecb6d256e77aa535a2d6a0684f60387e1780e